[font=Verdana][size=4]
{{COVER}}[center][size=7][b]Easter Eggs[/b][/size]
[size=5][b]Seasonal treasure hunts for your world.[/b][/size]

[b]6 ready-made hunts  ·  20 animated eggs  ·  20 particle effects[/b]
Hide collectibles, write clues, reward every milestone and crown the fastest hunters.

[url=https://docs.despical.dev/easter-eggs/gallery/][b]Watch the video gallery[/b][/url]  ·  [url=https://docs.despical.dev/easter-eggs/getting-started/][b]Get started[/b][/url]  ·  [url=https://docs.despical.dev/easter-eggs/][b]Read the documentation[/b][/url][/center]

Turn your spawn into an Easter garden, your ocean into a sunken treasure hunt, or your village into a haunted trail. [b]Easter Eggs lets you hide animated collectibles anywhere, decide how each hunt is played, and reward players fairly for every find.[/b]

Everything is managed from in-game editors, and every setting is also available in commented YAML files. Players get clear menus, written clues and progress they can follow, without ever seeing where an egg is hidden.

{{HR}}
[center][img]https://docs.despical.dev/images/easter-eggs/storefront/seasons.webp[/img][/center]

Five bundled eggs for every season: [b]spring[/b] baskets and golden eggs, [b]summer[/b] pearls and sunken treasure, [b]autumn[/b] pumpkins and ghosts, [b]winter[/b] presents and snow globes. Each one comes with its own particle effect and a matching hunt.

Global, Easter, Scuba, Halloween, Christmas and a timed [b]Enchanted[/b] challenge are installed for you. Place the eggs where you like, or create as many hunts of your own as you need.

{{HR}}
[center][img]https://docs.despical.dev/images/easter-eggs/storefront/tour.webp[/img]
[size=3]Recorded in Minecraft on a Paper server with the bundled templates and their default effects.[/size][/center]

[url=https://docs.despical.dev/easter-eggs/gallery/][b]Watch the full cinematic tour and all twenty clips →[/b][/url]

{{HR}}
[center][img]https://docs.despical.dev/images/easter-eggs/storefront/styles.webp[/img][/center]

Choose per template. A [b]placed head[/b] sits in the world like a real block. A [b]floating display[/b] rotates and bobs, with its own scale, spin and height. Switching later keeps every egg, its discoveries and its rewards.

[b]Twenty layered particle effects.[/b] Rings, spirals, orbits, bursts, hearts, stars and waves, each with editable colors, sizes, speed and timing. Give an egg one effect while it is hidden, another once it is found, one while its hunt is closed, and a private burst at the moment of discovery.

[center][img]https://docs.despical.dev/images/easter-eggs/storefront/particles.webp[/img][/center]

Per-player particle budgets keep busy areas smooth, and players can turn effects off for themselves.

{{HR}}
[center][img]https://docs.despical.dev/images/easter-eggs/storefront/hunt-rules.png[/img][/center]

[list]
[*][b]Free or ordered.[/b] Let players collect in any order, or turn the hunt into a trail where each egg unlocks the next.
[*][b]Timed challenges.[/b] Players start the clock, race to the last egg and set personal and server records. Choose whether the timer keeps running while they are offline.
[*][b]Personal or shared.[/b] Everyone finds every egg, or the first finder claims it for the current period.
[*][b]Schedules.[/b] Open and close a hunt on set dates in your time zone, announce it, and reward the top three when the season ends.
[*][b]Repeat periods.[/b] One-time events, daily or weekly resets, or a cooldown after completion.
[*][b]Entry requirements.[/b] Permissions, previously completed hunts or any PlaceholderAPI value, combined with all-of or any-of rules.
[/list]

{{HR}}
[center][img]https://docs.despical.dev/images/easter-eggs/storefront/hints.png[/img][/center]

Players can ask for a [b]written clue[/b] for their next egg. Give each egg its own clue or use the template's default. Optional [b]hot and cold[/b] feedback tells hunters when they are getting close. There are no arrows and no distances, so finding an egg still feels earned. An optional boss bar shows progress and time.

{{HR}}
[center][img]https://docs.despical.dev/images/easter-eggs/storefront/rewards.png[/img][/center]

Reward every egg, the first find, a number of eggs, a percentage, every few eggs, a full set of one egg type, completion, the first finishers, new records and final season ranks. Combine items, XP, Vault money, console or player commands, messages, broadcasts, titles, action bars, sounds, particles and fireworks in one reward, or let a [b]weighted pool[/b] pick a surprise.

[b]Nothing is paid twice.[/b] Every reward is recorded once per player and period, so reloads, relogs, retries and restarts never repeat it. Items that do not fit wait in a personal [b]reward inbox[/b], and interrupted deliveries are held for review instead of being guessed.

[url=https://docs.despical.dev/easter-eggs/rewards/][b]How rewards work →[/b][/url]

{{HR}}
[center][img]https://docs.despical.dev/images/easter-eggs/storefront/menus.png[/img][/center]

One command, `/eggs`, opens every hunt with its progress, collection, clues and rewards. Unfound eggs stay a secret.

[center][img]https://docs.despical.dev/images/easter-eggs/storefront/leaderboards.png[/img][/center]

[b]Rankings worth chasing:[/b] server totals, per hunt, the current period and the fastest finishes, in menus and through PlaceholderAPI for your scoreboards and holograms.

[center][img]https://docs.despical.dev/images/easter-eggs/storefront/inbox.png[/img][/center]

[b]Nothing gets lost.[/b] Overflow items wait in the reward inbox with reminders before they expire. Players choose their own particles, sounds, nearby hints and progress bar.

{{HR}}
[center][img]https://docs.despical.dev/images/easter-eggs/storefront/editor.png[/img][/center]

Open `/eggs admin`, choose a hunt and pick a template. You receive a placement head: put it down like any block and the egg is saved. Move an egg without losing its history, duplicate it, set its collection order, write its clue or switch the hunt's rules from the dashboard. Every action has its own permission, and every change is validated before it is applied.

[spoiler=Commands and permissions]
[b]Player commands[/b] (granted to everyone by default)
[list]
[*]`/eggs`: browse hunts. `eastereggs.menu`
[*]`/eggs start <hunt>` and `/eggs leave <hunt>`: start or leave a timed attempt. `eastereggs.start`, `eastereggs.leave`
[*]`/eggs hint <hunt>`: request a clue. `eastereggs.hint`
[*]`/eggs rewards <hunt>`: preview rewards. `eastereggs.rewards`
[*]`/eggs leaderboard [hunt]`: browse rankings. `eastereggs.leaderboard`
[*]`/eggs preferences`: personal effects and sounds. `eastereggs.preferences`
[*]`/eggs inbox`: claim waiting items. `eastereggs.inbox`
[*]Collecting eggs: `eastereggs.collect`
[/list]

[b]Administrator commands[/b] (operators by default, each with its own `eastereggs.admin.<command>` node)
[list]
[*]`/eggs admin`: open the hunt editor.
[*]`/eggs admin give <hunt> <template>`, `/eggs admin place`, `/eggs admin edit off`: placement.
[*]`/eggs admin move`, `copy`, `order <number>`, `hint <text>`, `remove confirm`: edit the egg you are looking at.
[*]`/eggs admin create <id> <name>`, `delete <hunt> confirm`, `set`, `clone`, `reload`: configuration.
[*]`/eggs admin preview <preset>`: preview a particle effect privately.
[*]`/eggs admin reset <hunt> <player-uuid|all> confirm`: reset attempts while keeping earned rewards.
[*]`/eggs admin deliveries`: review interrupted reward deliveries.
[*]`/eggs admin migrate <flat|mysql> <folder>`: import data from an older version.
[/list]

[url=https://docs.despical.dev/easter-eggs/commands/][b]Full command reference →[/b][/url]
[/spoiler]

{{HR}}
[center][img]https://docs.despical.dev/images/easter-eggs/storefront/storage.png[/img][/center]

[b]SQLite[/b] works out of the box, and [b]MySQL[/b] with verified TLS is built in. No extra database plugin is needed. Discoveries, rewards and rewards waiting to be delivered are saved together, so a crash never leaves a half-finished reward behind.

[b]Upgrading from an older version?[/b] Easter Eggs explains the steps in the console, makes a backup, imports your old egg types, locations and player discoveries, and writes a report. Imported history never pays rewards again.

[url=https://docs.despical.dev/easter-eggs/migration/][b]Migration guide →[/b][/url]

{{HR}}
[center][img]https://docs.despical.dev/images/easter-eggs/storefront/api.png[/img][/center]

A Bukkit service with immutable snapshots, non-blocking queries and [b]15 events[/b]: cancel collections, placements, starts and reward deliveries, or react to discoveries, completions and new records.

[spoiler=PlaceholderAPI placeholders]
[list]
[*]`%eastereggs_total%`, `%eastereggs_total_found%`, `%eastereggs_total_left%`
[*]`%eastereggs_hunt:<hunt>:found%`, `:left%`, `:percent%`, `:status%`, `:time%`
[*]`%eastereggs_leaderboard:global:<position>:name%` and `:value%`
[*]`%eastereggs_leaderboard:fastest:<hunt>:<position>:name%` and `:value%`
[/list]
[url=https://docs.despical.dev/easter-eggs/placeholders/][b]All placeholders →[/b][/url]  ·  [url=https://docs.despical.dev/easter-eggs/api/getting-started/][b]Developer API →[/b][/url]
[/spoiler]

{{HR}}
[center][img]https://docs.despical.dev/images/easter-eggs/storefront/start.png[/img][/center]

[b]Requirements:[/b] Paper or a compatible fork for Minecraft 1.21.11 to 26.3, and Java 25. PlaceholderAPI and Vault are optional. Folia is not supported.

[list=1]
[*]Place the JAR in your plugins folder and restart.
[*]Run `/eggs admin`, choose a hunt and pick a template.
[*]Place the head like a block, then run `/eggs admin edit off`.
[*]Let players type `/eggs` and start hunting.
[/list]

[url=https://docs.despical.dev/easter-eggs/getting-started/][b]Installation guide →[/b][/url]

{{HR}}
[center][size=6][b]bStats Metrics[/b][/size][/center]

Easter Eggs reports anonymous, aggregate usage statistics through [b]bStats[/b]. Disable it with `metrics: false` in config.yml.

[center][url=https://bstats.org/plugin/bukkit/Easter%20Eggs/21546][img]https://bstats.org/signatures/bukkit/Easter%20Eggs.svg[/img][/url][/center]

